{"body":"If I make a typo in the description is there a way I can modify that?\nSince the action is idempotent, then that implies the `String` is ignored.\n\n```rust\n    /// Add an artifact to the release.\n    ///\n    /// Idempotent — ignored if the CID already exists.\n    AddArtifact {\n        /// The content identifier for this artifact.\n        cid: Cid,\n        /// A human-readable description of the artifact.\n        name: String,\n    },\n```\n\nI would also create a struct:\n```rust\npub struct Artifact {\n    /// The content identifier for this artifact.\n    cid: Cid,\n    /// A human-readable description of the artifact.\n    name: String,\n}\n```\nAnd change the above to `AddArtifact(Artifact)`. The reason being that\nI would then create a smart constructor:\n```rust\nimpl Artifact {\n    pub new(cid: Cid, description: &str) -> Result<Self, ArtifactError> {\n      /* Add length constraints to `description` */\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIt would be preferable for the whole network if these string values\nwere not abused, and so we should limit size of data.","type":"comment"}